1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,300
Merge Sorted Array — LeetCode 88

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,600
Merge nums2 into nums1, in place

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,300
Naive idea: fill from the front

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,150
But that overwrites the unread 1

5
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:13,200
So fill from the back instead

6
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,620
Compare nums1[i] and nums2[j]

7
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,100
6 > 3 — place 6 in the last slot

8
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,400
5 > 3 — place 5

9
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,700
3 > 2 — place 3, taken from nums1

10
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:27,000
2 = 2 — ≤ picks nums2

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,700
j < 0, loop ends — 1 and 2 already sorted

12
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:33,400
Sorted in place · O(m + n) time, O(1) space
